1. Use minimum-of-N instead of median for the growth-shape ratio statistic. Positive-only noise (scheduler pauses, steal time) never lowers a minimum; genuine superlinearity shows up in the min of both sizes just as clearly (a quadratic does 4x the WORK — its min is its min). 
2. Increase runs from 5 to 9 for tighter min convergence.
3. Optionally raise base cells from 100k to 200k for the ASCII prose case so the timed window (~7ms/14ms) is further above the noise floor. The other two paths (CJK, hard-cut) are slower per cell so already less sensitive, but consistency is nice. Actually CJK 100k cells = 50k runes ≈ similar ms. Keep all three at the same change for uniformity — use min-of-9 for all growth tests.

